  "changes": "Background: three CC0 wood maps merged, then sampled through a periodic domain-warp flow field (FFT-filtered noise) so the grain bends; eight knots each pull the grain round them (sample rows move towards the knot row) and add growth rings and a dark heart; colour and tone drift from low-frequency noise; seamless. Timber pieces: planks with bevelled seams and butt joints, frame bars with carved groove, end-grain corner blocks with off-centre rings, pegs, nail heads, edge chips. Knotwork: (2,3) and (2,5) torus-knot projections and two-strand plaits drawn procedurally as shaded bronze tubes with an alternating over-under gap, embossed on corner caps, plait liner, divider, tab and button ends and the four corners of the timber button. Hover is a subtle warm edge.",
